Sound mixer batches, EE COP0 Count, IOP heap reuse.
- SPU2 mixer (sound_engine): mixBatch computes a batch voice by voice (a voice's state does not depend on the others
  within a batch; the dry mix is an integer sum) instead of 48 voice steps per frame. advanceTo only records the time and
  mixes once 64 frames (1.3 ms) are due; every LIBSD API call (set/get param, switch, address, core attribute, sample RAM,
  streams) first mixes what is due (flushPending), so the driver sees and changes the same state as before. GOW_SND_VERIFY=1
  mixes every batch also with the old per-frame step() and compares: 5.9 M frames, 0 differences. The mixer went from ~14 %
  to ~4 % of the game thread with sound on. GOW_SND_PERFRAME=1: the old per-frame path.
- COP0 Count: mfc0 / mtc0 Count read and set the EE cycle counter (PS2Runtime::eeCountRegister / setEeCountRegister)
  instead of ctx->cop0_count, which nothing advanced. God of War's 0x185A20 builds a 64-bit clock from Count and works
  until a per-frame deadline (0x781EC cycles, ~1.7 ms): with a frozen Count it did all pending work in one frame, as the
  God of War II port found in its loader (9ccffe1). GOW_EE_COUNT_FROZEN=1: the old value. Needs the recomp stage.
- IOP heap (iop_memory): first fit from the heap base, as the Killzone port's 0028; the search started at a cursor that only
  moved forward, so memory the IRX modules freed was never handed out again. QueryMaxFreeMemSize reports the largest gap;
  a failed allocation is logged ([iop-heap]). PS2X_IOP_HEAP_REUSE=0: the old allocator.
Measured on the ship with the launcher's defaults (with 10): combat average 56.5 -> 58.8 fps, minimum 51.4 -> 56.0;
GOW_VU1N_VERIFY clean, no IOP allocation failure, gameplay reached.

